WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.273 --> 00:00:01.690
SPEAKER: This
presentation focuses

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.420
on registering and preparing
for the Associate Cloud Engineer

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.010
Certification Exam.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:08.530
As you prepare for your
careers in a cloud-first world,

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.230
there's no better time
for you to get certified.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:13.330
Certification is essential
in today's market

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:16.329
to validate mastery and
competency of technologies

00:00:16.329 --> 00:00:19.270
that are critical to
business's success.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.820
Certification provides
credibility and industry

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.110
recognition.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.260
It is a testament to your skills
and proficiency in Google Cloud

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.550
Platform.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.380
Certification is a
formal recognition

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.170
of professionals who meet
established knowledge, skills,

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:33.940
or competencies.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.400
Certification often gives
you a competitive advantage

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.703
over somebody who
is not certified.

00:00:38.703 --> 00:00:40.120
Certification
ensures that you are

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.550
on top of industry and
technology developments

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:44.770
and that your
skills are updated.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.880
In 2013, 70% of IT professionals
believe that certifications

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.860
lead to a more effective staff.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.160
That number is well
above 90% today.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.660
One of our partners who took
the training and certifications

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.060
told us, GCP
certification proves

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:01.820
that an engineer not only
has real world experience,

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.470
but also has the
technical knowledge

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.780
to operate at the
level required.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.520
The Associate Cloud
Engineer Track

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:10.580
includes the Associate Cloud
Engineer Certification.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.580
This certification is an entry
point to a career in cloud

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.830
and to Google Cloud
certification.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.900
The Associate Cloud
Engineer Certification

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:19.670
assesses your
technical knowledge,

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:23.030
including the ability to
plan, deploy, and ensure

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.910
successful operation
of a cloud solution.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:27.560
Professional-level
certifications

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.140
identify individuals
who are capable of work

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.260
that is critical to modern
technology initiatives.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.600
We make sure that these
certification exams actually

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.730
validate role-related skills.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.290
They don't just assess
technical requirements

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.830
but also assess how you
map business requirements

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:46.010
to solutions developed
using Google Cloud.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.680
Hands-on practice is
critical to success.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.500
Exams must be taken at a
Kryterion-authorized. test

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.340
center.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.670
Register early, as test center
availability is limited.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.520
Questions can be multiple
choice or multiple select.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.310
You can go back and review
earlier questions at any time

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.240
during the exam.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.729
No paper, pens, or pencils
are allowed during testing.

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:10.919
In professional
exams, when answering,

00:02:10.919 --> 00:02:13.350
there might be several
options that seem correct,

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:14.940
but there is only
one option that

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:18.330
satisfies both technical
and business requirements.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.670
Choose the best, even if
the others might work.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:24.830
We are testing for
Google best practices.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:27.620
With Google Cloud certification,
you can differentiate yourself

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.180
from your peers.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.580
You also have the opportunity
to network and exchange

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.430
ideas in the Google Cloud
Certified community.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.170
Review the Exam
Guide to understand

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.470
the scope of the exam.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.320
Complete all courses in the
Architecting with Google Cloud

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.030
Platform Specialization.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.400
Spend sufficient time
to watch the videos,

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:49.180
complete all hands-on labs, and
review related documentation

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.120
in order to fully learn
concepts and practice working

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.280
with Google Cloud Platform.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:57.070
Hands-on experience is
critical to success.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.020
Practice with
additional hands-on labs

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.060
in the Qwiklabs platform.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.470
Complete the self-paced labs
in the Cloud Architecture

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:06.400
Quest and GCP Essentials Quest.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.240
You can also complete additional
labs on related topics.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.850
Note that you can complete
these labs free of charge.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.710
Check previous
communication sent to you

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.140
with Qwiklabs
credits information.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:20.690
Assess your knowledge by taking
the Associate Cloud Engineer

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:22.280
Practice Exam.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.950
You can take the practice
exam any number of times.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:28.110
Register early for
a certification exam

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:30.550
at the nearest Kryterion
Testing Center.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:32.460
You can find a Kryterion
Testing Center using

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.240
the locator website shown here.

